    "showPartitioning": false,
    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Projects stock day by day from on-hand, demand and open purchase orders to give run-out dates, shortfalls and what to expedite.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Supply Chain",
    "tags": [
        "stock projection",
        "run-out",
        "inventory",
        "purchase orders",
        "shortage",
        "days of cover",
        "supply chain",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Projects each item's stock **day by day** from stock on hand, expected **demand** (forecast or orders) and expected **receipts** (open purchase orders, transfers), and reports **when it runs out**.\n\n- **Input 1**: one row per item with stock on hand, and optionally a safety stock and a steady daily demand\n- **Input 2** (optional): dated future movements per item with a quantity and a type; types containing *receipt, PO, purchase, transfer in, supply* or *inbound* (your own list) are receipts, anything else is demand\n- Per item: **run-out date**, days until run-out, days of cover, first day below **safety stock**, lowest projected stock and **shortfall**, next receipt, and a **status**: *Runs out before next receipt*, *Runs out (receipts too small or late)*, *Below safety stock* or *OK*, sorted with the urgent ones first\n- The daily projection (opening, demand, receipts, closing) for charts\n\nPairs with Safety Stock and Reorder Point (the levels) and Holt-Winters Forecast (the demand).",
